#	/etc/unwind.blocklist — domains answered with REFUSED by unwind(8)
#
#	Referenced from /etc/unwind.conf:
#	    block list "/etc/unwind.blocklist" log
#
#	Syntax: one domain per line; a leading dot matches the zone and all of
#	its subdomains.  Blank lines and #-comments are ignored.
#
#	This is a *local* list for the gateway's own lookups.  Client-side
#	blocking belongs on the dns VM (unbound's local-zone/local-data), because
#	clients never talk to this instance.
#
#	The entries below are examples of the shape a lab blocklist takes, kept
#	deliberately small: a large third-party blocklist belongs in a cron job
#	that downloads it, not in a file maintained by hand.

# Vendor telemetry that phones home from lab hardware.
.telemetry.vendor.example
.metrics.vendor.example

# Public NTP, when the lab must use its own ntpd(8) for consistent logs.
pool.ntp.org
.time.nist.gov

# Ad networks — kept minimal here; see the note above.
.ads.example
